{"iter": 0, "slug": "baseline-no-adapter", "ts": "2026-05-18T21:11:00Z", "status": "kept-baseline", "family": "baseline", "rubric_version": "v1.2", "verdict": "Baseline established. 23 eval rollouts; 19 succeeded, 4 hit RemoteDisconnected/HTTP 500 from kiln-serve being restarted by an unrelated autonomous loop sharing the pod (pi-compaction-grpo-v062-h12). On the 19 clean rollouts, mean composite = 0.328 \u00b1 0.346; 7 tasks score ~0.71-0.81 (pi-format + content gate passes); 12 tasks score ~0.07 (format gate fail). Bimodal distribution \u2014 base model emits pi-format on ~37% of tasks, fails on the rest. Strong gradient signal target for GRPO.", "composite": 0.328, "composite_clean_n19": 0.328, "composite_raw_n23_with_errors": 0.276, "sub_scores": null, "training": null, "rollout_stats": {"n_eval_tasks": 23, "n_eval_rollouts": 23, "n_clean_rollouts": 19, "n_network_errors": 4, "clean_mean_composite": 0.328, "clean_stdev_composite": 0.346, "clean_min": 0.0683, "clean_max": 0.8074, "n_gate_pass_gt_0p5": 7, "n_gate_fail_lt_0p1": 12, "mean_wall_clock_s": 79.39}, "asi": {"what_worked": "End-to-end loop closes: pi-format prompt \u2192 kiln chat completion \u2192 multi-component rubric. Strong bimodal signal \u2014 7/19 base rollouts pass the gate. The variance across the bimodal distribution gives GRPO clear gradient.", "what_failed": "Pod-sharing conflict with an unrelated pi-compaction-grpo autonomous loop on the SAME RunPod pod. That loop's bootstrap (process 567) restarted kiln serve mid-eval \u2014 4 tasks hit RemoteDisconnected or HTTP 500. The kiln-pool architecture has no per-tenant isolation; once the pod is leased, anything previously scheduled on it (including other lab bootstraps) can also run.", "next_focus": "iter 1: H1 default GRPO recipe on 12 shorter training tasks (source_text < 100K chars to keep rollout time bounded). Pre-registered in hypotheses/h1-default-recipe-iter1.md. Falsification threshold: composite uplift >= +0.05 over iter 0 baseline 0.328 on a clean re-eval."}, "kiln_polish_noted": true, "git_sha": "d7658770"}
{"iter": 1, "slug": "h1-default-recipe-truncated", "ts": "2026-05-18T22:10:00Z", "status": "rollouts-only-training-too-slow", "family": "H1", "rubric_version": "v1.2", "verdict": "Training rollouts succeeded \u2014 48 rollouts on 12 short tasks (source_text < 100K chars), source truncated to last 30K chars. Mean composite 0.558 (vs iter 0 baseline 0.328 on full source). 4 of 12 groups passed strong-signal filter (var > 0.05). GRPO training step kicked off with KILN_GRAD_CHECKPOINT_SEGMENTS=8, lr=1e-5, rank=16. After 6 min still no progress lines in log \u2014 pi compaction has rollouts ~4x more tokens per group than pi-doctest (avg ~33K total tokens per group vs ~19K for pi-doctest), making GRPO step too slow for pod TTL.", "composite": null, "training": {"lr": 1e-05, "rank": 16, "alpha": 32, "groups_seen": 12, "groups_kept_after_filter": 4, "filter_var_threshold": 0.05, "grad_checkpoint_segments": 8, "training_killed_after_min": 6, "killed_reason": "pod TTL budget \u2014 full training projected at ~120 min on these long-context groups"}, "rollout_stats": {"n_train_tasks": 12, "n_train_rollouts": 48, "train_mean_composite": 0.558, "train_p50_composite": 0.748, "train_mean_wall_clock_s": 26.12, "strong_signal_groups": 4, "tasks_with_pure_pass": 6, "tasks_with_pure_fail": 2, "tasks_with_recoverable_signal": 4}, "asi": {"what_worked": "Truncating source_text to last 30K chars made rollouts tractable (26s mean wall vs 80s+ on full source). Strong-signal filter identified 4 groups with clear pass/fail variance \u2014 the recoverable cases where GRPO would have strongest gradient. The framework end-to-end works.", "what_failed": "GRPO training step on pi-compaction-sized rollouts is prohibitively slow even with shorter source. Each group has ~30K tokens of context (truncated source + completion); 4 groups = 120K tokens, plus the recurrent GDN backward which dominates wall time on long sequences. Pi-doctest had ~3K tokens per group total, ~10x less.", "next_focus": "Iter 2 should EITHER (a) further truncate source to ~5K chars (matching the v062 lab's 1200-char approach) and reduce max_response_tokens to ~1024 to make GRPO step fit in <10 min, OR (b) wait for a kiln-train optimization that handles long-context completions more efficiently. The framework + iter 0 baseline + iter 1 rollouts are committed to the kiln branch; the trained adapter is the unfinished piece."}, "kiln_polish_noted": true, "git_sha": "45120203"}
